0	section	Interrogation
0	section	Talking to the Prince or Sergeant
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Ah, nilsal, sergeant.
1	line	Sergeant Tobyn	Prince Itzla! I... I'm sorry, but I wasn't expecting you here.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Well all that politics downstairs was getting a bit dry, but then I heard there'd been a bit of a commotion. I thought I'd come see what the fuss was all about. You don't mind, do you?
1	line	Sergeant Tobyn	Well no, it's just...
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Wonderful! And you! Who are you?
1	line	Player	Hello there. I'm {player}.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	{player}? Kuaini! Pleased to meet you. Crown Prince Itzla Arkan, heir to the Sun Throne, at your service.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Tell me, {player}, are you the one who caught these would-be assassins?
1	line	Player	That's right.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Well then, why don't you and I ask this one a few little questions. You don't mind, do you, sergeant?
1	line	Sergeant Tobyn	Not at all, but...
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Excellent! Let's get started then.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Nilsal to you, iknami. I hear you managed to get yourself into a spot of bother.
1	line	Bandit	I'm not telling you anything.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Ah, tetamo! Such a shame. No matter though! We'll have you talking in no time.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Now, you'll need to forgive me, but I'm a bit new around here, so your customs are not familiar to me. Tell me, iknami, what's the preferred method of interrogation in these parts?
1	line	Bandit	You're asking me how you should interrogate me?
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Well it just seemed polite to ask. We have all sorts of fun methods back home in Varlamore. We could give one or two of them a go if you want?
1	line	Bandit	If I want?
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Absolutely! Now, what are your thoughts on chicken?
1	line	Bandit	Chicken?
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Oh, {player}, do you not have chickens here? Sorry, again, all this is quite new to me.
1	line	Player	Yes, we have chickens. The farms around here have loads.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Well then, why the confusion? Have you never seen one before? Oh you poor sheltered thing. Did your parents never show you the wonders of the countryside?
1	line	Bandit	I know what a chicken is!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Well why didn't you say so?
1	line	Bandit	I don't know what game you're playing, but it won't work on me!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	No game at all, iknami. The reason I ask is because one of our preferred methods in Varlamore involves just a small amount of fire, and you'd never believe it, but the smell of human flesh once it gets going...
1	line	Bandit	You're going to cook me?
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Cook? No, not at all! That would imply I'm going to eat you, and I'm not a barbarian! Though, it would be interesting to know if it tastes like chicken as well...
1	line	Bandit	Alright, enough! I'll tell you what you want!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Kuaini!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	So who are you working for?
1	line	Bandit	I don't know their name. They just paid us to attack the delegation. They didn't look to be from around here. I reckon it was one of your lot!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Why did they want you to attack the delegation?
1	line	Bandit	They didn't say, but that priest... he was the target!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	So a Varlamorian paid you to assassinate the Teokan? You're not giving me much to go on.
1	line	Bandit	That's all I know!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Hmm...
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Well I think we're done here. Come, {player}.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	I think we got what we needed there.
1	line	Sergeant Tobyn	You're sure he told you everything?
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Oh yes. The fear of being cooked will do that to a person. All total rubbish of course! Imagine burning someone alive! We're much more civilised over in Varlamore.
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	We just cut out their heart while it's still beating instead.
1	line	Player	I can't tell if you're joking or not...
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Anyway, sounds like there'll be some work to do when we get back home. An assassination attempt on the Teokan of Ralos... Concerning stuff. First up though, I'd better get back to the politics!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	{player}, once we've got these papers signed, you lot will be free to travel to Varlamore for the first time! No more needing explicit permission. You can come and go as you please!
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Now, it's entirely up to you of course, but given we have you to thank for stopping this plot, I'd be very keen if you'd join me in Varlamore to continue the investigation.
1	cond	Before the release of Varlamore:
2	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	No need to decide now. It will take a bit longer for us to be ready for visitors anyway, but when the time comes, I'll have my people send word to you.
2	action	continue
1	cond	After the release of Varlamore:
2	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	No need to decide now, but if you do wish to accept my offer, just speak to Regulus Cento outside the eastern gates of this city.
2	action	continue
1	line	Prince Itzla Arkan	Now, they'll be missing me downstairs. Timoiva, and may the sun light your way!
1	box	Itzla departs.
1	line	Sergeant Tobyn	Well, that was interesting...
1	line	Player	Not every day the heir to a far-off land comes and interrogates one of your prisoners?
1	line	Sergeant Tobyn	Oddly enough, no. This will be an interesting report to write. And on that note, I'd best get to it. All the best, adventurer. Thank you for your help.
